🛡️ Penetration Test Report: eCommerce Order API

Target: api.ecom-store.com/v1/orders

Scope: API endpoints responsible for fetching customer order details.

1. Executive Summary

This report details a Critical Risk finding stemming from a Broken Access Control (Insecure Direct Object Reference, or IDOR) vulnerability in the core eCommerce API. An authenticated user can bypass authorization checks and view sensitive personal and financial information belonging to other customers simply by manipulating the order_id parameter in a GET request.

Key Findings Identified:

Critical Risk: IDOR allows horizontal privilege escalation to view private order data.

Data Impact: Full customer names, shipping addresses, order contents, and the last four digits of the payment method are exposed.

